V. THE X-4: A LARGE QUADROTOR MAV
The X-4 Flyer consists of a chassis, rotors, motors, power cells and avionics. Each subsystem is listed in the weightbudget, Table I, and described below. Component distances are measured with respect to the rotor plane, (masses ±0.005 kg, distances ±0.005 m) (see Fig. 2).
A. Chassis
The X-4 has an aluminium centre frame with carbon fibrefoam sandwich arms. Motors and batteries are mounted as far from the central axis as possible to slow the pitch and roll dynamics. The arms angle down slightly to provide more clearance between the bottom of the arms and flapping rotor
